<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Hello all that OpenGD77 Team,<br><br>Just to let you know the following issue.<br><br>I've got a Retevis RT-82 and I've loaded both versions of firmware:<br><br>This one (latest):<br><br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/MD2017/Firmware/0f43e6cdffe5cd6ac6ce14eb1506c1c815dbb341" class="postlink">downloads/MD2017/Firmware/0f43e6cdffe5c ... c815dbb341</a><br><br>Does have an audio problem.<br><br>The previous one:<br><br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/MD2017/Firmware/049e598c09c247d77d96c620aaad3dcd1eb07016/" class="postlink">downloads/MD2017/Firmware/049e598c09c24 ... d1eb07016/</a><br><br>Is working just fine.<br><br>The audio problem is that the speaker - either via the Internal or via a SpeakerMic - stops working a minute or so after power on. I've consulted thoroughly the manual but did not found any speaker time out parameter. Also it happens in both DMR or FM, in Double Watch or simple VFO mode.<br><br>I can not emphasize enough how grateful I am for the brilliant work the team as done: My Retevis is now a completely new radio. Bought it 2nd hand in early 2018 and with this firmware the possibilities are incredible wider than with the original Firmware. THANK YOU!<br><br>All best from IM58 and 73,<br><br>Antonio Cochicho<br>(CT7ARF)</div></blockquote>I have a Retevis RT-82 running with 20240412 firmware and I have not detected any audio problem.<br><br>What ECO level do you use ?<br><br>I do have another problem with audio level in FM mode as it's much weaker than before.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2867">SA0BUX</a> — Mon May 06, 2024 7:11 am</p><hr />
